{"name":"Mayflower Orchid","hex":"#ed93d7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mayflower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants that flower in May - especially the hawthorn (in Britain) and the trailing arbutus (in the US)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mayflower"},{"term":"orchid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the orchid family (Orchidaceae), bearing unusually-shaped flowers of beautiful colours. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A light bluish-red, violet-red or purple colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a light purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Laelia speciosa","blocks":[{"text":"Laelia speciosa, also known as the Mayflower orchid, is a species of orchid from Mexico. It flowers between March and October, and has white-tipped purple blossoms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Laelia_speciosa.jpg/330px-Laelia_speciosa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laelia_speciosa","wikidata":"Q1318039"},{"title":"Mayflower","blocks":[{"text":"Mayflower was an English square-rigged merchant sailing ship, active from before 1609 until 1622. Her tonnage was 180+, and she was 110 feet long and 25 feet in the beam, with several decks. She was notable in that she transported a group of English families, known today as the Pilgrims, from England to the New World in 1620."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Copyrighted_and_Published_by_A_S_Burbank%2C_The_Mayflower_at_Sea_%28NBY_21340%29.jpg/330px-Copyrighted_and_Published_by_A_S_Burbank%2C_The_Mayflower_at_Sea_%28NBY_21340%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayflower","wikidata":"Q187093"},{"title":"Orchid","blocks":[{"text":"Orchids are plants that belong to the family Orchidaceae, a diverse and widespread group of flowering plants with blooms that are often colourful and fragrant. Orchids are cosmopolitan plants, living in diverse habitats on every continent except Antarctica. The world's richest diversity of orchid genera and species is in the tropics. Many species are epiphytes, living on trees. The flowers and their pollination mechanisms are highly specialized, attracting insect pollinators by colour, pattern, scent, pheromones, and sometimes by mimicking female insects. Orchids have very small seeds, relying on fungal partners for germination. Some orchids have no leaves, either photosynthesizing with their roots or relying entirely on fungal partners for food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid","wikidata":"Q25308"},{"title":"Orchid (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Orchid is a bright rich purple color that resembles the color which various orchids often exhibit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Labiata.jpg/330px-Labiata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid_(color)","wikidata":"Q1925148"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Isaac_Claesz._Van_Swanenburg_Washing_the_Skins_and_Grading_the_Wool.jpg/500px-Isaac_Claesz._Van_Swanenburg_Washing_the_Skins_and_Grading_the_Wool.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Isaac_Claesz._Van_Swanenburg_Washing_the_Skins_and_Grading_the_Wool.jpg/500px-Isaac_Claesz._Van_Swanenburg_Washing_the_Skins_and_Grading_the_Wool.jpg?utm_sourc